      "content": "Using leftover antibiotic eye drops outside of their intended time frame could potentially cause more harm than good, including antibiotic resistance or an allergic reaction. It's important to prioritize this health concern despite the inconvenience. The symptoms might not seem significant now, but using antibiotics inappropriately can have long-term implications. I strongly advise against using them.\n\nA safer approach would be to refrain from using them and try to rest your eyes until morning. If symptoms like increased pain, blurred vision, or discharge develop, promptly seek professional medical help. The risk of complications typically outweighs the worry of needing a quick visit to urgent care. Your health should always be the top priority.",
