    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand your concern about your eye discomfort and the urge to take immediate action. However, it's not advisable to self-prescribe medication, even if it's just a small amount of something that was previously prescribed to you. Eye infections and serious conditions like keratitis can escalate quickly, and inappropriate use of antibiotics can have serious consequences, such as promoting resistant bacteria.\n\nA more responsible approach would be to contact a medical professional through a telehealth service if possible. Most providers can offer guidance and may even prescribe a suitable eye drop for you to use until you can see them in person.\n\nIf acute symptoms worsen or you cannot reach a medical professional promptly, it would be advisable to at least go to urgent care to get a professional examination to prevent potential serious complications. Your vision and the overall health of your eyes should not be jeopardized by self-treatment without proper authorization. Remember, it's always better to be cautious with your health, particularly when it comes to your eyes.",
